#preface([Preface])[
These notes are a companion to the theory-focused _QFT Notes_ (Weinberg-style).
The goal here is different: every result is earned by explicit calculation.
Conceptual motivation is kept minimal; the emphasis is on doing the algebra,
regularizing divergences, extracting finite answers, and building intuition
through the mechanics of the calculation itself.

The progression is chosen to maximize computational payoff early:
path integrals first, then free fields (including finite temperature),
then interactions via $phi^3$ before moving to realistic theories.

Prerequisites: classical field theory, special relativity, quantum mechanics,
and basic complex analysis (contour integration).
]
